From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:38:23 +0200
Subject: net: dsa: lantiq: ask for what the xRX500 switch needs to probe

The reset lines of the integrated PHYs come from the SoC's own reset
controller. Its driver has no prompt outside COMPILE_TEST and defaults to a
system type this family is not, so it can only arrive by selection -- and a
configuration line naming it does not survive, because a promptless symbol
falls back to its default whatever the file says. On this platform it was
being selected by an unrelated PHY driver; turn that driver off and every
reset lookup defers forever, the switch never probes and the board has no
network at all, with nothing in the log naming the cause.

The driver that needs it asks for it now, together with the register window
the reset controller reads its status through, and both only on the system
type that has this switch. The firmware loader the integrated PHYs are
staged through is asked for too, and the memory-mapped regmap both switch
models build on moves to the core they share.

Also drop a comment's reference to a file this tree does not have; the
register it describes is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/Kconfig b/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/Kconfig
index 7c13df0a0dc7..fc9ddad11b9a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/Kconfig
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 config NET_DSA_LANTIQ_COMMON
 	tristate
 	select REGMAP
+	select REGMAP_MMIO
 
 config NET_DSA_LANTIQ_GSWIP
 	tristate "Lantiq / Intel GSWIP"
@@ -13,10 +14,22 @@ config NET_DSA_LANTIQ_GSWIP
 
 config NET_DSA_LANTIQ_GSWIP_XRX500
 	tristate "Lantiq / Intel GSWIP 3.0"
+	depends on INTEL_MIPS || COMPILE_TEST
 	depends on HAS_IOMEM
 	depends on RESET_CONTROLLER
+	select FW_LOADER
 	select NET_DSA_TAG_GSWIP3
 	select NET_DSA_LANTIQ_COMMON
+	#
+	# The reset lines of the integrated PHYs come from the SoC's own
+	# reset controller, whose driver has no prompt of its own and
+	# defaults to a system type this family is not. Without it every
+	# reset lookup defers forever and the switch never probes, so the
+	# one driver that needs it asks for it, along with the register
+	# window it reads its status through.
+	#
+	select MFD_SYSCON if INTEL_MIPS
+	select RESET_LANTIQ if INTEL_MIPS
 	help
 	  This enables support for the two Lantiq / Intel GSWIP 3.0 switch
 	  macros found in the xRX500 SoC family.
